# crud — the OLTP home turf (report-class; SQLite's strong regime, benched to lose honestly)

Seed 1. One shared op stream per family, folded by both engines; the read query oracle-gated (value-identical multisets) on every lane before any timed window. ratio = ours p50 / sqlite p50 (lower is better; <1 = bumbledb faster).

## lane durable

Db::create (LMDB issues F_FULLFSYNC unconditionally on macOS) vs SQLite WAL synchronous=FULL fullfsync=ON checkpoint_fullfsync=ON, cache_size=-262144, temp_store=MEMORY, whole-file mmap (coverage asserted), wal_autocheckpoint=0 — both engines flush to media on every commit

| family | about | ours p50 (µs) | sqlite p50 (µs) | ratio | ours p99 (µs) | sqlite p99 (µs) |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| crud_read_point | keyed point read: (id, val) by key, 3 hits + 1 miss rotation | 0.79 | 1.92 | 0.41 | 0.92 | 2.17 |
| crud_insert | one fresh Doc row per commit (fsync-bound single-writer floor) | 5030.92 | 4548.42 | 1.11 | 6133.21 | 5613.75 |
| crud_insert_10 | 10 fresh Doc rows per commit | 5239.83 | 4463.00 | 1.17 | 6950.67 | 6268.04 |
| crud_insert_100 | 100 fresh Doc rows per commit | 8540.29 | 4487.17 | 1.90 | 11211.42 | 5306.17 |
| crud_insert_1k | 1000 fresh Doc rows per commit | 20057.42 | 5126.83 | 3.91 | 26540.58 | 5464.08 |
| crud_update | one keyed Counter value replacement per commit | 5138.83 | 4279.83 | 1.20 | 5319.88 | 5476.25 |
| crud_update_hot | the same replacement pinned to one hot row (key 0 every sample) | 5143.25 | 4205.17 | 1.22 | 6840.12 | 5216.04 |
| crud_upsert | keyed upsert over twice the Counter mass (~half miss) | 5124.33 | 4252.88 | 1.20 | 5596.17 | 5354.71 |
| crud_rmw | read-modify-write round trip: point read, host +1, write back | 5140.92 | 4236.08 | 1.21 | 5619.08 | 5328.25 |
| crud_delete | one pool-row delete per commit (delete-bearing by contract) | 5125.58 | 4287.92 | 1.20 | 5744.79 | 6062.12 |
| crud_mixed_90_10 | 9 point reads + 1 single-row insert commit per sample | 5134.33 | 4286.54 | 1.20 | 6286.46 | 5354.21 |

## lane nosync

Db::ephemeral (MDB_NOSYNC: pages and meta pwritten, no sync boundary ever crossed) vs SQLite WAL synchronous=OFF fullfsync=OFF checkpoint_fullfsync=OFF, cache_size=-262144, temp_store=MEMORY, whole-file mmap (coverage asserted), wal_autocheckpoint=0 — WAL frames written, never synced (OFF, not NORMAL: NORMAL still syncs at checkpoints, which would cross-match a store kind that never syncs)

| family | about | ours p50 (µs) | sqlite p50 (µs) | ratio | ours p99 (µs) | sqlite p99 (µs) |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| crud_read_point | keyed point read: (id, val) by key, 3 hits + 1 miss rotation | 0.50 | 1.21 | 0.41 | 0.54 | 1.38 |
| crud_insert | one fresh Doc row per commit (fsync-bound single-writer floor) | 28.46 | 16.58 | 1.72 | 38.42 | 33.79 |
| crud_insert_10 | 10 fresh Doc rows per commit | 82.17 | 21.92 | 3.75 | 108.04 | 60.46 |
| crud_insert_100 | 100 fresh Doc rows per commit | 521.25 | 115.79 | 4.50 | 567.67 | 186.75 |
| crud_insert_1k | 1000 fresh Doc rows per commit | 4402.21 | 699.79 | 6.29 | 4755.12 | 749.00 |
| crud_update | one keyed Counter value replacement per commit | 30.46 | 10.25 | 2.97 | 40.79 | 61.08 |
| crud_update_hot | the same replacement pinned to one hot row (key 0 every sample) | 27.21 | 9.58 | 2.84 | 32.62 | 13.29 |
| crud_upsert | keyed upsert over twice the Counter mass (~half miss) | 24.67 | 15.42 | 1.60 | 34.38 | 77.75 |
| crud_rmw | read-modify-write round trip: point read, host +1, write back | 28.04 | 10.46 | 2.68 | 34.79 | 14.08 |
| crud_delete | one pool-row delete per commit (delete-bearing by contract) | 23.92 | 16.08 | 1.49 | 26.42 | 36.67 |
| crud_mixed_90_10 | 9 point reads + 1 single-row insert commit per sample | 31.46 | 30.12 | 1.04 | 43.67 | 66.62 |

post-state: Doc + Counter value-identical across engines, both lanes. Every row above is report-class, never gated — no budget gate reads a crud number.
